Z||000002||Eddie.H||01-26-2000||07:22 PM||||ITS 1993 Z34 5 SPEED I WOULD POST PICS BUT I WORK ON A MAC AND I CAN NOT USE PIP AND THE PICS ARE AT HOME ANY WAY BUT CAN I USE THAT 5 SPEED OR NOT||||reg||1
Z||000003||olympic||01-26-2000||08:11 PM||||  Thats a good(and expensive) tranny. Its a little stronger than the getrag in the fiero but the problem is that it has a wierd clutch.  The clutch fork works in the opposite direction than a fiero(pull instead of push.) I believe this requires a custom fabricated slave cylinder setup. I'd go with this tranny if possible because it is stronger and probably has better gear ratios for the hi revving 3.4 TDC.<P>BTW, the Fiero 5 speed was the getrag 282, the 5 speed in the Lumina was the getrag 284.<p>[This message has been edited by olympic (edited 01-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||william_thorniii||01-26-2000||08:27 PM||||Eddie,<P>No reason to get upset.  I was only amazed.  Do you have any idea how rare that car is?  Anyway, I think that it will work with Rodney Dickmans FWD transmission mount.  His site is <A HREF="http://www.execpc.com/rodney~1" TARGET=_blank>www.execpc.com/rodney~1</A>   His stuff is all laser cut, very high quality and at a good price.  Ask him if his bracket works for your specific application.  I am sure that he will be able to answer you better than any of us!<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||12
